A||N||8||Butter||Windows 2000 Wallpaper help||||5||
Z||000000||Butter||12-13-2001||04:53 PM||||Could anyone direct me on how to turn a picture file into wallpaper on a Windows 2000 operating system?||||reg||5
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||12-13-2001||05:00 PM||||Right-Click on your existing background (a menu will pop up... select properties). Default shoud show you the "Background" tab.  Click the "Browse" button and locate the picture you want to use.  Then select it and set your "picture display" setting to whatever works best (ususally center or stretch depending on the photo).  Then click the "OK" or "Apply" button to make it active!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Loki||12-13-2001||05:10 PM||||Well, one cool thing I like about Xp is right click on pic, and hit make background   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Bout the only thing I like   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroloki.com/lokisig1%20copy.jpg">   <BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
Z||000003||Butter||12-13-2001||05:13 PM||||MinnGreenGT,<BR>I copied a picture from the Tennessee Titans (the flaming T) and could not get the computer to read the file right.  It would show a small picture of it in Explorer but give me an file reading error when I tried to open it.  It will not highlight the wall paper option as my older Windows NT version will allow when I right click on it.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||12-13-2001||05:26 PM||||Butter- It must not be in a compatible format...?  If you have photoshop (or similiar) double check that the format is either JPG or BMP (or other common format). Or re-download (is that a word?) from the website and save it as a different filename (could have errored during download).<P>Loki... I had forgotten about that- Win 2000 is the same way.  I can right click on any picture (even in an explorer window) and select "set as Wallpaper" -Good call.||||reg||1
